<title>SOUTH KOREA: BOK sees dlr at peak vs won in current conditions.</title>
<headline>BOK sees dlr at peak vs won in current conditions.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>An assistant governor of the central Bank of Korea (BOK) said on Tuesday he believed the dollar had peaked against the won given the current demand and supply situation.</p>
<p>The dollar hit its historic high of 901.00 won at 0130 GMT, but soon fell to 899.70 won after the central bank intervened by selling dollars.</p>
</text>
